WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:11.720
We are putting a complete siege on Gaza.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:14.472
No electricity...

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.892
no food, no water, no gas.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:19.102
It's all closed.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.649
We're fighting animals and are 
acting accordingly.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.319
That was the defense minister of Israel...

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:32.032
responding to the deadly attack 
on October 7th by Hamas...

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:34.075
a militant group based in Gaza.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.913
Hamas launched rockets, 
killed over 1,400 civilians...

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:41.249
and kidnapped close to 200 people.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.587
Within days, Israel bombarded 
the Gaza Strip...

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:49.174
killing several thousand, 
wiping out entire families...

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:52.135
and striking ambulances, 
border crossings...

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:53.845
and residential buildings.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:58.266
At the same time, Israel 
told over 1 million civilians...

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.226
to leave their homes and move south.

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:03.438
Warning them of an escalation 
of violence in the north.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:06.983
But Israel is bombarding the south, too.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:09.903
Leaving Palestinians trapped.

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:12.947
For as long as this conflict has existed...

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.658
movement in and out of the Gaza Strip...

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:19.662
has been, to one degree or another, 
restricted.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:24.459
The prime minister of the Israeli occupation, 
Benjamin Netanyahu...

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:27.128
he knows very well

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:28.463
that people are not able to leave.

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:43.520
The Gaza Strip is the smaller of 
the two Palestinian territories

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.231
occupied by Israel since 1967.

00:01:47.023 --> 00:01:51.402
This sliver of land only 25 miles long 
and 7.5 miles wide...

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:54.072
is home to over 2 million Palestinians.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:57.909
Making it one of the most densely 
populated areas in the world.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.662
For the last 16 years

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:03.331
residents here have been living 
under a harsh blockade...

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:07.335
that allows Israel to control 
the flow of electricity, fuel

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:09.462
food, water, and medical supplies.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.966
So they can dictate when 
Palestinians receive essentials...

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:14.717
and when they're denied.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.639
That control is rooted in 
violence and destruction...

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.975
that goes back decades.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.437
Before the establishment of Israel...

00:02:26.729 --> 00:02:30.650
Gaza was part of what became known as 
historic Palestine...

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.028
under Ottoman rule and later 
under British occupation.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.032
In 1947, as the British prepared to leave...

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:39.826
they left the fate of Palestine...

00:02:40.034 --> 00:02:42.078
up to a newly formed United Nations...

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:45.123
who voted to divide Palestine 
into a Jewish state...

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:46.583
and an Arab state.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:51.004
Soon, Zionist forces and militias 
began to forcibly expel

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.381
hundreds of thousands of Palestinians 
from their land...

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.508
to establish the state of Israel.

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:59.095
Many internally displaced Palestinians

00:02:59.095 --> 00:03:00.805
fled to this narrow stretch of land...

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.100
that would later become known as 
the Gaza Strip.

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:07.604
So these refugees became 
refugees because...

00:03:08.646 --> 00:03:11.274
they were pushed out of their 
towns and villages.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:13.943
Some of them literally live 
a mile away from

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:15.778
what used to be their 
towns and villages.

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:19.657
Many others were forced to flee 
to neighboring Arab countries.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.035
Overwhelmed by refugees...

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.495
these countries immediately declared a war

00:03:24.495 --> 00:03:27.999
against the new state of Israel 
to support Palestinian Arabs.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.501
They eventually lost to Israel...

00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:33.296
but Jordan ended up occupying 
the West Bank 

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:36.216
and Egypt occupied Gaza City 
and nearby towns 

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.884
along these ceasefire lines.

00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:41.596
Then in 1967...

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.181
another war broke out.

00:03:44.807 --> 00:03:46.517
Amid Palestinian resistance

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:49.062
and fearing threats from neighboring 
Arab countries...

00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:53.441
Israel launched a full scale attack 
on Jordan, Syria, and Egypt.

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:55.151
In just six days...

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:58.363
Israel captured the Gaza Strip 
and the Sinai from Egypt...

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:01.908
the West Bank from Jordan and 
the Golan Heights from Syria.

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:06.287
This was the beginning of 
the Israeli occupation in Gaza...

00:04:06.537 --> 00:04:07.914
that continues today.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.460
Israel took control of all movement 
from and to the Gaza Strip...

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.504
by land, air, and sea.

00:04:15.046 --> 00:04:18.258
It placed troops along this line 
and inside the Gaza Strip...

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:21.469
and allowed Palestinians to travel 
between the Gaza Strip...

00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:24.013
Israel, the West Bank, 
and East Jerusalem.

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:26.724
But just a few months after the war

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:29.519
even though Palestinians now lived 
under Israeli control...

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:34.274
they began to be referred to as 
“non-citizens” or “foreign residents”

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.067
in official Israeli documents.

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:40.238
You inherit the status from 
your parents and grandparents.

00:04:40.822 --> 00:04:44.826
Being a stateless, unrecognized, 
with no rights...

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.578
and you know this impacts your life.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:51.249
This was also when Israel 
started to build settlements

00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:53.793
for Jewish Israelis inside of Gaza.

00:04:54.085 --> 00:04:55.169
To Palestinians...

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.214
this meant even more land 
being taken away from them.

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:01.009
And they were being closed in.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.927
Israel did not allow Palestinians here

00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:05.013
to operate their own seaport or airport.

00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:07.390
Within the Gaza Strip...

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:11.060
Israel developed key industries 
like agriculture...

00:05:11.352 --> 00:05:13.938
to cater to Israeli and 
West Bank markets...

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:16.899
taking advantage of Gaza's 
cheap labor market

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:19.027
and paying Palestinians very little.

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:22.113
These economic challenges led to the rise

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:23.990
of a prominent Islamic social charity:

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.200
Mujama al-Islamiya.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.621
At the time, this charity, 
partially funded by Israel...

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.832
built schools, mosques, clinics 

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.501
and provided more food 
for Palestinians in Gaza.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.879
But tensions simmered.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.423
Israel feared a growing 
resistance movement.

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.092
And in response, soldiers often frisked...

00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:45.261
arrested and detained residents.

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:50.350
In 1987, that tension reached 
a breaking point

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.353
after an Israeli truck crashed 
into a civilian car...

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.438
killing four Palestinians.

00:05:57.106 --> 00:05:59.275
Palestinians immediately responded

00:05:59.275 --> 00:06:02.070
with protests, strikes, and boycotts 
against occupation.

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:05.198
It would become known as 
the first uprising...

00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:06.991
or intifada. 

00:06:08.159 --> 00:06:09.369
And that same year

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:13.623
Mujama al-Islamiya transformed 
into a militant group: Hamas.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:16.667
Hamas was a group that came about

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.628
during the first Palestinian uprising.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.255
And was not really a part

00:06:21.255 --> 00:06:23.007
of institutional politics 
for some time.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:26.636
They weren't in charge of Gaza yet,
but they wanted to liberate

00:06:26.636 --> 00:06:28.971
Palestinian territories from Israel's control...

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.641
and considered Israel 
an illegitimate state.

00:06:32.517 --> 00:06:34.477
After the first year of the intifada...

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:38.189
during which over 140 Palestinians 
in Gaza were killed...

00:06:38.481 --> 00:06:42.485
Hamas and other militant groups 
began to attack Israelis more directly.

00:06:43.486 --> 00:06:46.280
Then the intifada grew more violent in 1991...

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:49.575
which is also when Israel introduced 
a permit system

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:52.412
that greatly restricted Gaza residents’ 
ability to work...

00:06:52.703 --> 00:06:53.746
travel through Israel...

00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:56.374
or access the West Bank 
and East Jerusalem.

00:06:57.542 --> 00:06:59.085
By the end of the First Intifada...

00:06:59.335 --> 00:07:02.422
Israeli forces had killed over 
1,000 Palestinians...

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:06.259
and Palestinian militants had killed 
over 100 Israelis...

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:08.761
throughout Israel and 
the occupied territories.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.474
The uprising ended after the 
internationally brokered 

00:07:13.474 --> 00:07:14.559
Oslo Peace Accords...

00:07:14.684 --> 00:07:18.146
between Israel and the Palestine 
Liberation Organization...

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:19.689
or the PLO.

00:07:20.982 --> 00:07:23.443
This was a liberation movement 
with an armed wing...

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.529
that fought for Palestinian rights 
for decades.

00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:31.325
The PLO agreed to disarm and recognize 
Israel's right to exist.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:34.745
But Hamas, which had very little 
political support at the time

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:36.164
strongly opposed it.

00:07:36.706 --> 00:07:39.125
The deal also created a new governing body:

00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:41.502
The Palestinian Authority, or PA...

00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:45.047
which allowed political parties
and elections in the Gaza Strip.

00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:48.426
The PA was granted some autonomy 
within small areas...

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:50.887
but Israel still controlled the territories

00:07:50.887 --> 00:07:52.847
and the flow through these crossings.

00:07:54.432 --> 00:07:55.516
The Oslo agreement

00:07:55.516 --> 00:07:58.394
also promised Palestinians 
some level of autonomy...

00:07:58.603 --> 00:08:00.897
and a path to statehood in five years.

00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:03.858
But that never happened.

00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:06.986
Instead, what followed was 
more Israeli settlements

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.279
on Palestinian land.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.242
And a year later, following an attack 
by an Israeli settler in the West Bank

00:08:13.242 --> 00:08:15.912
and a series of bombings by 
Palestinian militants

00:08:15.912 --> 00:08:17.038
including Hamas...

00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:20.124
Israel’s prime minister called for 
the construction of a fence

00:08:20.124 --> 00:08:21.083
around the Gaza Strip.

00:08:22.919 --> 00:08:25.630
Gaza now had a physical barrier 
between it

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.839
and the outside world.

00:08:28.758 --> 00:08:30.343
These moves made Palestinians

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:33.846
trust the Israeli government and 
peace negotiations even less...

00:08:34.388 --> 00:08:36.974
and it would lead to a second uprising.

00:08:42.438 --> 00:08:44.357
On September 28th, 2000

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:47.860
Israeli politician Ariel Sharon visited 
Al-Aqsa mosque...

00:08:48.319 --> 00:08:49.820
a muslim holy site in Jerusalem

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:53.074
that's largely inaccessible to Palestinians 
in the Gaza Strip.

00:08:54.075 --> 00:08:57.203
This visit sparked widespread protests 
and violent clashes...

00:08:57.787 --> 00:09:02.416
resulting in Israeli forces killing four 
Palestinian children the next day.

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:06.879
And Palestinian militants carried out 
suicide bombings.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:09.882
Back in the Gaza Strip...

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:12.802
Palestinians broke down much of this barrier.

00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:15.638
The Israeli government soon
built it back up

00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:19.517
and heavily militarized it with more troops 
and observation posts.

00:09:20.101 --> 00:09:22.645
They further canceled travel 
and work permits...

00:09:22.979 --> 00:09:26.190
restricting movement through 
this crossing even more....

00:09:26.524 --> 00:09:29.318
and eventually destroyed Gaza's 
only major airport...

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.445
and its under-construction seaport.

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.907
By the end of the Second Intifada in 2005...

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:38.536
Palestinian militants had 
killed over 900 Israelis...

00:09:38.953 --> 00:09:41.914
and Israeli forces killed over 
3000 Palestinians.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:45.251
The Second Intifada gradually 
came to an end...

00:09:45.459 --> 00:09:49.130
as Israel dismantled all Jewish Israeli 
settlements in the Gaza Strip...

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:50.965
and withdrew the ground troops.

00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:55.511
Then another internationally brokered 
agreement gave the PA

00:09:55.511 --> 00:09:58.514
control of this crossing with Egypt 
on the Gaza side...

00:09:59.682 --> 00:10:02.018
and allowed trucks and convoys 
to flow between

00:10:02.018 --> 00:10:03.519
the Gaza Strip and the West Bank.

00:10:04.478 --> 00:10:06.314
But Israel didn't let that happen.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:11.694
At the time of the first legislative election 
after the Second Intifada...

00:10:11.861 --> 00:10:14.655
Fatah, a party backed by 
the PA and PLO...

00:10:14.822 --> 00:10:17.491
that had negotiated with Israel, 
was in power.

00:10:18.826 --> 00:10:22.413
But many Palestinians saw Fatah 
and its approach as ineffective.

00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:24.790
Hamas, which was now 
a political party

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.542
in addition to being a militant group...

00:10:26.834 --> 00:10:29.337
won most of the seats in 2006.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:36.594
People voted for Hamas as a way to...

00:10:36.761 --> 00:10:38.095
to express their disapproval

00:10:38.095 --> 00:10:39.597
of the ongoing status quo

00:10:39.597 --> 00:10:41.140
which was that the peace process 
had failed

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.185
and they had had two uprisings 
and no state was in sight.

00:10:44.727 --> 00:10:47.313
In response to an armed 
militant party winning...

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:50.316
Israel banned laborers from 
leaving Gaza for work.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.694
Then, when militants captured 
an Israeli soldier...

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:55.863
Israel carried out airstrikes in Gaza...

00:10:56.197 --> 00:10:58.199
and tightened its control on the sea

00:10:58.199 --> 00:11:01.452
limiting fishing capabilities 
to only six miles.

00:11:02.411 --> 00:11:05.748
Politically, within Gaza, 
Hamas had won the election...

00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.042
but the PA was still 
the governing body...

00:11:08.292 --> 00:11:09.835
with Fatah under its wing.

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:13.297
A conflict broke out between 
Hamas and Fatah...

00:11:13.547 --> 00:11:16.842
and Hamas seized power 
of the entire strip in 2007.

00:11:17.968 --> 00:11:19.887
This is when Israel put Gaza

00:11:19.887 --> 00:11:22.682
under the official blockade 
that continues today...

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.559
tightening Israel's grip 
over Gaza even more...

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:28.729
trapping over 2 million Palestinians inside.

00:11:29.605 --> 00:11:32.733
This time, Israel closed the main crossing 
for commercial goods...

00:11:33.275 --> 00:11:34.860
made travel even more restrictive...

00:11:35.152 --> 00:11:36.862
banned exports from Gaza...

00:11:36.904 --> 00:11:39.907
and imposed restrictions on 
the import of essential items...

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:42.618
such as fuel, medicine, and food.

00:11:43.285 --> 00:11:45.413
They even used mathematical formulas...

00:11:45.663 --> 00:11:48.165
to determine the necessary caloric intake...

00:11:48.416 --> 00:11:51.752
for people in Gaza to control
how much food they would allow in.

00:11:52.294 --> 00:11:54.922
Basically, we live a slow death 
in Gaza.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.633
Even before major escalations.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.802
People cannot travel freely.

00:12:00.594 --> 00:12:02.263
We have Israeli drones...

00:12:02.471 --> 00:12:04.306
hovering around 24/7.

00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:06.559
There's always stress.

00:12:07.017 --> 00:12:08.477
Over the next several years

00:12:08.477 --> 00:12:10.730
reoccurring conflicts and airstrikes 

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:14.024
made the already devastanting impacts
of this blockade worse.

00:12:14.984 --> 00:12:17.737
Israeli airstrikes destroyed vital infrastructure...

00:12:17.945 --> 00:12:19.822
such as water and power plants.

00:12:20.197 --> 00:12:21.949
Repairs were delayed by the blockade...

00:12:22.199 --> 00:12:24.952
which impacted the delivery 
of construction materials.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.289
And for each militant attack on Israelis...

00:12:28.664 --> 00:12:31.876
Israel killed far more Palestinians 
in retaliation.

00:12:37.965 --> 00:12:40.801
At times, Israel would slightly lift restrictions...

00:12:41.051 --> 00:12:44.305
but it was never close to matching
the humanitarian needs

00:12:44.305 --> 00:12:45.765
of Palestinians in Gaza.

00:12:47.808 --> 00:12:50.144
According to a UN report from 2022...

00:12:50.394 --> 00:12:52.188
The 16 year blockade had made 

00:12:52.188 --> 00:12:55.065
78% of the water in Gaza undrinkable...

00:12:55.357 --> 00:12:59.779
left 62% of Palestinians inside of Gaza
in need of food assistance...

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.697
living with rolling power cuts

00:13:01.697 --> 00:13:04.366
that last on average 
11 hours per day.

00:13:05.242 --> 00:13:07.244
That is our normal life.

00:13:07.995 --> 00:13:11.707
We would have 8 hours of electricity, 
12 hours of electricity...

00:13:11.749 --> 00:13:14.293
It changes depending on the situation

00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:16.796
and the availability of fuel. 

00:13:18.172 --> 00:13:20.132
We are completely dependent on Israel.

00:13:21.258 --> 00:13:23.260
This is what many Palestinians

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.680
and international law calls 
collective punishment.

00:13:27.014 --> 00:13:31.352
Collective punishment is when 
cancer patients cannot travel...

00:13:31.644 --> 00:13:33.312
because they get denied.

00:13:33.854 --> 00:13:34.647
And collective punishment...

00:13:34.814 --> 00:13:38.359
It means also that Palestinians
cannot have their own hospitals...

00:13:38.359 --> 00:13:39.610
and they cannot treat...

00:13:40.653 --> 00:13:41.570
their patients.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.322
Collective punishment means 

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.866
the people of Gaza now are punished...

00:13:47.201 --> 00:13:48.994
for the most recent escalation.

00:13:51.121 --> 00:13:52.957
When you look at the crime of genocide...

00:13:53.249 --> 00:13:56.293
which is, you know, the 
intentional destruction...

00:13:56.418 --> 00:13:58.838
of a whole people in part or in whole.

00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:02.758
We are seeing elements 
of that crime

00:14:02.758 --> 00:14:05.219
being committed and carried out 
in the Gaza Strip...

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:06.095
right now.

00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:07.221
There's equating...

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.808
between Hamas and all Palestinians.

00:14:11.058 --> 00:14:13.018
And this is not the first time

00:14:13.018 --> 00:14:15.604
that we're going to see people in Gaza

00:14:15.604 --> 00:14:18.357
and civilians in Gaza, 
half of whom are children...

00:14:18.983 --> 00:14:21.277
pay the price for Hamas 
or anything else.

00:14:22.027 --> 00:14:24.113
Israeli and US leaders
have emphasized

00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:25.865
that Israel has a right to defend itself...

00:14:26.198 --> 00:14:28.200
by wiping out Hamas completely.

00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:31.871
But the majority of casualties
in the Gaza Strip...

00:14:32.496 --> 00:14:33.747
aren't Hamas fighters.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.749
They're civilians.

00:14:36.458 --> 00:14:38.252
It's an interesting question

00:14:38.252 --> 00:14:39.920
to consider whether or not...

00:14:40.629 --> 00:14:43.549
things would have been different 
if Hamas didn't exist.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:47.261
But the thing is, Hamas didn't exist 
until the late 80s.

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:49.930
But the occupation of the Palestinian territories

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:51.348
has been since 1967.

00:14:51.891 --> 00:14:55.352
And the original Palestinian displacement 
was 1948.

00:14:55.477 --> 00:14:58.230
And Hamas didn't really emerge until much later than that.

00:14:58.731 --> 00:15:00.900
I think that anybody who follows

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:04.278
Israeli and Palestinian politics 
with some level of honesty...

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.323
knew that if...

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:08.699
what happened 
hadn't happened

00:15:08.699 --> 00:15:09.992
something else was going to happen...

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.036
because the status quo 
was unsustainable.

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.705
The world has to recognize this suffering.

00:15:15.456 --> 00:15:17.291
Even before we have escalations.

00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:19.543
The reason we have escalations 
is because...

00:15:19.877 --> 00:15:21.295
people cannot find any hope.

00:15:22.504 --> 00:15:24.381
No one wanted to get to this point.

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:26.717
The tragedy of it all in my mind...

00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:28.719
I think, besides the loss of human life...

00:15:29.136 --> 00:15:32.222
is that it was preventable, 
easily preventable.

